      <h1>China Battery Exports: The 2024-2025 Time Series</h1>
      <p class="muted">Battery Market Intelligence · Data period 2024–2025 (customs/industry) · Last reviewed 2026-09-16</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Direct answer:</strong> China's lithium-battery exports reached <strong>US$61.1 billion in 2024</strong>
        — <strong>53.4% of the global export total</strong> — and grew to <strong>US$76.8 billion in 2025</strong>.
        In H1 2025 alone China exported <strong>2.16 billion cells, +17.6% year-on-year (US$34.1 billion)</strong>.
        The structure is shifting: the <strong>EU takes ~40%</strong> while <strong>US imports fell</strong> from
        $15.3B to $11.9B.
      </div>
